WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.669
 Steven, Cade, congratulations.

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:05.137
You guys have made it into
the third and final round

00:00:05.204 --> 00:00:07.106
of this competition, and
let me say this-- you

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:08.207
fellas can forge, man.

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:10.042
You guys really
brought your A game.

00:00:10.109 --> 00:00:11.711
But you're going to
have to step it up,

00:00:11.778 --> 00:00:13.946
because now we're sending
you back to your home forges

00:00:13.979 --> 00:00:16.683
to recreate this iconic
weapon from history.

00:00:19.385 --> 00:00:22.021
The Rooster Head
French Pioneer Sword.

00:00:22.087 --> 00:00:24.157
[rooster crowing]

00:00:24.958 --> 00:00:26.025
Gentlemen, good luck.

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:27.227
We'll see you in four days.

00:00:32.131 --> 00:00:33.832
CADE: We're here in
Loranger, Louisiana,

00:00:33.899 --> 00:00:36.369
and I'm ready to get going.

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:38.705
We're going to try to
whack this piece of metal

00:00:38.738 --> 00:00:41.507
out and get it into profile.

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:43.176
I start off at the
tip because it's

00:00:43.243 --> 00:00:47.914
probably the most demanding, and
I work my way back from there.

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:51.551
Traditionally, these blades
have a slight saber type bend

00:00:51.617 --> 00:00:54.387
in them, so I heat
it up, and I whack

00:00:54.453 --> 00:00:55.922
it over the end of the anvil.

00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:59.959
I'm very tired, but I got
the forging of my blade done.

00:01:00.026 --> 00:01:01.494
While I'm waiting
for it to cool off,

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:03.729
I'm just going to go and work
on my rooster head pommel.

00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:04.731
I found this chicken head.

00:01:04.797 --> 00:01:05.998
I thought it would be perfect.

00:01:06.031 --> 00:01:10.069 line:0%
So I can make the mold
to cast with bronze.

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:11.571 line:0%
It wasn't able to
heat treat, but

00:01:11.638 --> 00:01:14.507 line:0%
what I didn't get done on the
blade, I got down on my mold.

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:17.643 line:0%
So I still feel
like I'm on track.

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:19.278 line:0%
STEVEN: So it's the
morning of day two,

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:21.347 line:0%
and I've got a lot
of work to do today.

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:24.984
I have to cut my saw
teeth into the back.

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:26.486
Now I'm ready for
the heat treat.

00:01:26.552 --> 00:01:28.888
This is proving a little
more difficult than I thought

00:01:28.921 --> 00:01:30.290
it'd be to get an even heat.

00:01:37.329 --> 00:01:38.831
This plate isn't all that hard.

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:42.168
[bleep],, can't turn in a
blade that's half hard.

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:43.903
I am screwed.

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:45.471
So here we go again.

00:01:45.537 --> 00:01:47.239
I'm going to sit here
and re-quench this,

00:01:47.306 --> 00:01:49.175
and re-straighten
this until it's hard.

00:01:54.813 --> 00:01:55.981
There's some flames.

00:01:56.048 --> 00:01:58.351
That's what we want to see.

00:01:58.417 --> 00:02:03.123
I file test it, skating my
glass That's a hard blade.

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:08.060 line:0%
CADE: I'm starting off the
day grinding my fullers.

00:02:08.127 --> 00:02:09.495 line:0%
Don't know how
that's going to go.

00:02:09.561 --> 00:02:12.165 line:0%
One danger of having
double sided fullers--

00:02:12.231 --> 00:02:14.567 line:0%
you can grind straight
through your blade.

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:16.202
And so I just kind
of go down the blade

00:02:16.235 --> 00:02:20.006
and check, and make
sure I'm not doing that.

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:21.574
I've got to sharpen
the saw back, too.

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:23.509
I don't know what they're
going to test this thing on.

00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:27.313
Hopefully it'll hog
away some stuff.

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:30.550
Now that I'm done with that,
it is time to heat treat.

00:02:36.088 --> 00:02:38.357 line:7%
It's hard.

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:41.294
 Today I'm going to
try to conquer casting.

00:02:41.361 --> 00:02:44.430
This is my absolute first
time doing any casting,

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:47.466
so hopefully I can
get it figured out.

00:02:47.533 --> 00:02:49.334
I want to cast three pieces.

00:02:49.368 --> 00:02:51.804
There's the guard piece,
handle, and then there's

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:53.406
the rooster headed pommel.

00:02:53.472 --> 00:02:56.376
My first casting is
just a piece of bronze

00:02:56.409 --> 00:02:59.812
that's going to be the guard
with the up-swept quillons.

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:00.980
All right.

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:03.149
That's way more than
enough for a guard.

00:03:03.216 --> 00:03:05.451
I have the guard cast, which
I'm pretty happy about.

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:08.821
I have the handle cast,
then I got this rooster.

00:03:08.888 --> 00:03:12.692
I can see an eye, I can see the
detailed feathers on this side.

00:03:12.759 --> 00:03:13.892
Friggin' sweet.

00:03:13.959 --> 00:03:16.162
This is a lot denser and heavier
than I thought, which I'm

00:03:16.229 --> 00:03:19.032
happy about because my blade
is super forward heavy,

00:03:19.098 --> 00:03:20.867
and I want that
balance point to just

00:03:20.933 --> 00:03:22.802
get farther back on the blade.

00:03:22.868 --> 00:03:25.805
Going into day four, I have
the three pieces of my handle.

00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:28.607
So my day tomorrow is
going to be tedious.

00:03:28.674 --> 00:03:30.910 line:7%
Finish work.

00:03:30.977 --> 00:03:32.578 line:0%
CADE: It's the
morning of day four,

00:03:32.644 --> 00:03:36.449 line:0%
and today it's just
putting it all together.

00:03:36.516 --> 00:03:39.552
I casted my rooster
head and my guard.

00:03:39.586 --> 00:03:43.656
And if I may say, this
is one bomb chicken head.

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:44.323
[rooster crows]

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:45.891
Look at that bad boy.

00:03:45.924 --> 00:03:49.095
Cock-a-doodle-doo.

00:03:49.161 --> 00:03:52.131
Handle comes next.

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:53.165
That's about it.

00:03:53.232 --> 00:03:54.767
Everything's
looking pretty good.

00:03:57.303 --> 00:03:59.672
 I got a sword!

00:03:59.739 --> 00:04:00.740
 All right, bladesmiths.

00:04:00.806 --> 00:04:04.043
Your blades look lovely,
but are they deadly?

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:05.477
I'm going to take your
weapons to deliver

00:04:05.544 --> 00:04:09.649
some lethal cuts and slashes
on this goat carcass.

00:04:09.715 --> 00:04:12.285
It's time to find out if
they're ready for a cockfight,

00:04:12.352 --> 00:04:14.053
or are they going
to play chicken?

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:14.953
Steven, you're up first.

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:15.821
Are you ready for this?

00:04:15.888 --> 00:04:16.656
 Let's do it.

00:04:19.191 --> 00:04:21.794
[chopping]

00:04:22.795 --> 00:04:25.331
[music playing]

00:04:40.612 --> 00:04:43.215
 All right, Steven, let's
talk about your sword here.

00:04:43.282 --> 00:04:46.219
It's beautiful looking,
and it's a heavy sword.

00:04:46.285 --> 00:04:49.354
But that lends itself
to deliver very

00:04:49.421 --> 00:04:51.124
deep cuts with every swing.

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:53.693
And more importantly,
it will kill.

00:04:56.161 --> 00:04:57.196
All right, Cade, your turn, sir.

00:04:57.263 --> 00:04:57.997
You ready?

00:04:58.064 --> 00:04:59.732
 Yes, sir.

00:04:59.799 --> 00:05:02.134
[chopping]

00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:05.705
[music playing]

00:05:20.787 --> 00:05:23.389
 All right, Cade, let's
talk about your sword here.

00:05:23.456 --> 00:05:26.659
Your handle construction
fits perfectly in my hand.

00:05:26.726 --> 00:05:31.798
Now, your edge is pristine, no
glints, no rollings whatsoever.

00:05:31.864 --> 00:05:34.867
And most importantly,
it will kill.

00:05:34.933 --> 00:05:37.637
 All right, gentlemen,
welcome to the strength test.

00:05:37.704 --> 00:05:39.672
The log chop.

00:05:39.706 --> 00:05:41.540
Now, to test the strength
and overall durability

00:05:41.607 --> 00:05:44.276
of your blades, I'll be
chopping on this log.

00:05:44.343 --> 00:05:45.511
All right, Steven,
you're up first.

00:05:45.578 --> 00:05:46.312
You ready for this?

00:05:46.379 --> 00:05:47.913
 Let's do it.

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:50.316
[chopping]

00:05:50.383 --> 00:05:53.886
[music playing]

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:08.701
 Right.

00:06:08.734 --> 00:06:10.569
First off, Steven, nice
job on the castings.

00:06:10.603 --> 00:06:11.670
They're nicely done.

00:06:11.737 --> 00:06:14.506
Your handle is about
an inch too long.

00:06:14.573 --> 00:06:17.510
It allows my hand to
travel around a lot.

00:06:17.576 --> 00:06:20.212
Your blade took no
damage whatsoever.

00:06:20.279 --> 00:06:21.013
Good job.

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:22.248
 Thanks.

00:06:22.315 --> 00:06:23.649
 All right, Cade,
you're up next.

00:06:23.683 --> 00:06:24.149
You ready?

00:06:24.216 --> 00:06:25.884
 Yes, sir.

00:06:25.951 --> 00:06:28.821
[chopping]

00:06:28.888 --> 00:06:31.791
[music playing]

00:06:46.672 --> 00:06:51.043
 All right, Cade, your
blade is in good condition.

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:52.611
No rolls, no chips.

00:06:52.645 --> 00:06:54.680
Still sharp as it
was when I started.

00:06:54.714 --> 00:06:55.748
Good job.

00:06:55.815 --> 00:06:57.416
 All right, bladesmiths,
this is the sharpness test--

00:06:57.483 --> 00:07:00.520
the scarecrow saw and slice.

00:07:00.586 --> 00:07:02.388
To test the saw
backs on your weapon,

00:07:02.455 --> 00:07:03.889
I'll be sawing into
the wooden dowels.

00:07:03.923 --> 00:07:06.525
Then I'll test the edge
by cutting the watermelon

00:07:06.592 --> 00:07:08.628
and a sugar cane bundle.

00:07:08.661 --> 00:07:09.828
Steven, you're up first.

00:07:09.862 --> 00:07:10.329
You ready?

00:07:10.396 --> 00:07:13.332
 Let's do it.

00:07:13.399 --> 00:07:16.268
[sawing]

00:07:16.335 --> 00:07:19.439
[music playing]

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:37.756
 All right, Steven, let's
talk about your saw back here.

00:07:37.823 --> 00:07:39.825
Once it gets started,
it starts to saw.

00:07:39.892 --> 00:07:40.759
It works.

00:07:40.792 --> 00:07:42.228
It's a functional
saw back in there.

00:07:42.295 --> 00:07:43.863
You're able to dig
into the dowel.

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:45.631
Your edge is sharp.

00:07:45.664 --> 00:07:47.666
No issues cutting
on the watermelon,

00:07:47.733 --> 00:07:51.537
and the weight alone is going to
just chop that whole thing off.

00:07:51.570 --> 00:07:53.739
Overall, sir, it'll cut.

00:07:53.806 --> 00:07:55.273
 Thank you.

00:07:55.340 --> 00:07:56.308
 All right, Cade, your turn.

00:07:56.375 --> 00:07:57.109
You ready?

00:07:57.176 --> 00:07:58.777
 Yes, sir.

00:07:58.844 --> 00:08:01.180
[sawing]

00:08:01.247 --> 00:08:04.150
[music playing]

00:08:16.862 --> 00:08:18.564
 All right, Cade, the saw back.

00:08:18.597 --> 00:08:20.799
These teeth are sharp.

00:08:20.866 --> 00:08:22.701
Even at the start,
it already digs in.

00:08:22.768 --> 00:08:25.537
A couple of slices in
there, it's already digging

00:08:25.604 --> 00:08:27.173
right into the wooden dowel.

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:29.608
Your edge-- no
issues whatsoever.

00:08:29.675 --> 00:08:32.478
Cuts through the watermelon,
and cuts the rest

00:08:32.545 --> 00:08:34.179
of the sugar cane bundles.

00:08:34.246 --> 00:08:36.047
Overall, sir, it'll cut.

00:08:36.114 --> 00:08:37.216
 Thank you.

00:08:37.283 --> 00:08:38.851
 All right, bladesmiths, the
weapons tests are complete

00:08:38.885 --> 00:08:41.553
and the judges literally
had to weigh the details.

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:43.789
The new "Forged in
Fire" champion is--

00:08:46.992 --> 00:08:48.093
Cade.

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:50.262
Congratulations, you are the
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:08:50.329 --> 00:08:54.600
Steven, your blade is 2 pounds
heavier than Cade's blade,

00:08:54.633 --> 00:08:56.002
making it less wieldy.

00:08:56.068 --> 00:08:59.171
Additionally, your handle is
a little bit out of proportion

00:08:59.237 --> 00:09:02.207
with the blade, and it's for
that reason that you cannot be

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:03.542
the "Forged in Fire" champion.

00:09:03.609 --> 00:09:06.479
Come on forward, my friend.

00:09:06.546 --> 00:09:08.314
 Even though I feel
somewhat defeated right now,

00:09:08.381 --> 00:09:09.881
I'm still proud
of what I've done,

00:09:09.915 --> 00:09:11.617
and I'm proud of
what I turned in.

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:12.717
- [inaudible].
- Thank you.

00:09:12.784 --> 00:09:13.952
 You're a great competitor.

00:09:14.019 --> 00:09:14.820
 Thank you.

00:09:14.887 --> 00:09:15.988
 Steven, this cast
is [inaudible]..

00:09:16.055 --> 00:09:17.489
 I'm not going to
say I'm going to go

00:09:17.556 --> 00:09:18.891
home and start making
swords, but I did

00:09:18.924 --> 00:09:20.726
really enjoy the whole process.

00:09:20.793 --> 00:09:22.695
And it also taught me what
I could do in a short amount

00:09:22.762 --> 00:09:25.998
of time, Not that it's my best
work, but I'm proud of myself

00:09:26.065 --> 00:09:29.134
for not giving up there.

00:09:29.201 --> 00:09:30.602
 Cade, congratulations.

00:09:30.669 --> 00:09:32.137
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion,

00:09:32.204 --> 00:09:36.275
and that is a title that comes
with a check for $10,000.

00:09:36.342 --> 00:09:37.977
How do you feel right now?

00:09:38.044 --> 00:09:38.877
 Cock-a-doodle-doo?

00:09:38.944 --> 00:09:41.113
[laughter]

00:09:42.248 --> 00:09:43.315
 Good job, my friend.

00:09:43.382 --> 00:09:45.751
You made a fine Rooster
Headed French Pioneer Sword.

00:09:45.818 --> 00:09:48.253
Come on forward
and shake our head.

00:09:48.286 --> 00:09:49.989
 I am super psyched right now.

00:09:50.055 --> 00:09:52.925
I am so proud of
myself, and I thank God

00:09:52.958 --> 00:09:54.793
that I had this opportunity.

00:09:54.826 --> 00:09:57.396
I gotta keep working
hard, and keep on trying

00:09:57.429 --> 00:09:58.630
to climb that ladder, you know?

00:09:58.697 --> 00:10:01.433
10 grand is college funds.

00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:03.135
[laughs]

